WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.708 --> 00:00:08.367
This gallery collects scholar media for the course: the researchers you are reading, speaking for themselves.

2
00:00:08.368 --> 00:00:16.286
Filter by week or by kind. Each card names the scholar, what the item explains, and why it is worth your minutes.

3
00:00:16.286 --> 00:00:27.290
Play inside the page or follow the link out. Embeddable videos use official platform players and nothing loads until you press play. Podcasts and restricted media link out to the source site.

4
00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:38.300
Use the watch-for prompts. Each card tells you what to watch or listen for, and which reading move to make next. A talk is a way into a source, not a replacement for reading it.

5
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:47.327
Write the note on the card. After the media, write one sentence you can prove from the reading. It lands in your weekly notes file.

6
00:00:47.327 --> 00:00:50.465
Watching is never tracked or graded.

7
00:00:50.465 --> 00:00:55.892
Where next: Open the reading the video connects to in Readings and Media.
